* Add the long-mode machine state and passage page.

  Selected by __x86_64__ / CONFIG_X86_64, with the existing 32-bit definitions
  moved into the #else. Explicit widths throughout, since this page is shared
  between an LLP64 host driver and an LP64 guest kernel.

  Offsets are generated from the compiled layout rather than hand-counted, and
  all 40 are asserted, as are sizeof == 0x140 and 16-byte alignment.

  Also adds co_param_t, the width of one passage-page parameter word, so that
  shared code can name it instead of assuming unsigned long -- which is 4 bytes
  on Win64 and truncates.

  The guest address window is provisional and unexercised; see the comment.

